<title>SLOVAKIA: SLOVAK CBANK SAYS C/A DEFICIT TARGET ACHIEVABLE.</title>
<headline>SLOVAK CBANK SAYS C/A DEFICIT TARGET ACHIEVABLE.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-05-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Slovakia (NBS) said on Monday it considered its ceiling for the current account deficit of five percent of full year 1997 GDP as being achievable.</p>
<p>&quot;There are some optimistic signs in the development of the trade balance so we consider the desired level of current account deficit of five percent of GDP as achiebvable,&quot; NBS Vice-governor Marian Jusko told Reuters.</p>
</text>
